WEBVTT


00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:01.440
This was the campaign we did

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:03.800
to celebrate 40 years of Renoir cinema.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:05.840
The briefing that came to us was something like

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.840
we want to find the answer to

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.240
what is cinema,

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.680
1 question as open as it cost

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:12.800
find 1 insight

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.360
and relevant to connect with the user.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:16.200
We did not want

00:00:16.201 --> 00:00:18.961
to stay in what everyone already knows about cinema.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.000
We needed to look differently to put the viewer

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.400
at the Center and remind him that cinema is not only seen,

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:26.194
is lived. 

00:00:26.194 --> 00:00:28.800
Because we weren't really talking about cinema,

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.160
we were talking about who lives it,

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:32.160
of those who cry without expecting it,

00:00:32.161 --> 00:00:33.681
of whom he recognizes himself in 1 story even if it is not his own,

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.320
of who leaves the room different from how he entered,

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.880
of who discovers other worlds he did not know.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:37.560
And we change

00:00:37.561 --> 00:00:40.241
the point of view of thinking about what is happening on the screen

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:41.880
to what happens in the armchair.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:44.880
Because everything that happens to us in our armchair is also cinema.

00:00:44.881 --> 00:00:46.300
And from this point on, 

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:47.601
were we able to answer

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:48.960
what is cinema?

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.082
Cinema is you. 

00:00:50.082 --> 00:00:51.760
And that's how we build the idea,

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:53.520
1 spot that opens each session

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.280
in all Renoir movie theaters,

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.200
social networks that created conversation

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.080
what cinema is all about

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:00.120
and assets

00:01:00.121 --> 00:01:03.161
designed to reinforce the message and at the same time

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.520
encourage subscription

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:06.360
to Renoir's membership club.

00:01:06.361 --> 00:01:08.081
Sometimes we can look for 1 creative concept,

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:08.496
, 

00:01:08.496 --> 00:01:09.360
elegant,

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:10.154
complex, 

00:01:10.154 --> 00:01:10.840
when in fact

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:12.560
All we have to do is

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:14.400
walk away 1 little and change the look
